Changes for 1.0.0 — 2026-05-24

Initial release of sevenx_payment_stripe.
Complete rewrite of the payment gateway: Authorize.Net replaced by Stripe.

New features
- Stripe Payment Element integration via Stripe.js v3.
  Supports cards, Apple Pay, Google Pay, Link, and all payment methods
  enabled in the Stripe Dashboard — no additional code required per method.
- PaymentIntents API: charge.php creates a Stripe PaymentIntent server-side
  and returns the clientSecret to the browser.
- confirm.php: Stripe return_url handler. Retrieves the PaymentIntent from
  Stripe directly (never trusts redirect_status URL param) and calls
  $order->modifyStatus(1000) on success, creating an atomic status history
  entry in eZ Publish.
- Stripe Tax Calculations API integration in charge.php. Tax is computed
  per line item using the customer shipping address. Non-blocking: a Stripe
  Tax failure logs via eZDebug and checkout continues without tax.
- buildLineItemsFromOrder(): converts eZ Publish product collection items
  into Stripe Tax line item arrays with amount, reference, and tax_code.
- Order ownership check: charge.php returns HTTP 403 if the authenticated
  eZ Publish user does not own the submitted order ID.
- loadForm() STATUS_ACCEPTED: detects order status_id === 1000 and returns
  eZWorkflowEventType::STATUS_ACCEPTED to advance the eZ Publish shop
  workflow without re-rendering the payment form.
- Idempotent confirm.php: skips modifyStatus() if order is already at
  status 1000, preventing duplicate history entries on repeated visits.
- module.php: registers both 'charge' (JSON endpoint) and 'confirm'
  (return_url handler) views under the 'charge' module.
- stripe.ini.append.php: INI-based configuration for SecretKey and
  DisplayHelp. Compatible with eZ Publish siteaccess override system.
- stripe-checkout-v4.js: Payment Element mounting, confirmPayment() call,
  return_url configuration.
- Generic error responses: PHP exceptions from the Stripe SDK are logged
  via eZDebug::writeError() and only a generic message is returned to the
  browser. No stack traces or internal details are exposed.

Security
- Card data never touches the server (Stripe.js hosted iframe).
- Server-side PaymentIntent verification before any order mutation.
- Order ownership enforced in charge.php (HTTP 403 on mismatch).
- Secret key stored in INI file only; never in PHP source or JS.
- PHP exceptions redacted from client-facing error responses.

Bug fixes
- PHP 8 deprecation fixed: eZOrder::active() required parameters moved
  before optional parameters (kernel/classes/ezorder.php and all callers).

Removals (legacy Authorize.Net integration)
- Removed: classes/ezauthorizeaim.php
- Removed: classes/ezauthorizeinfo.php
- Removed: classes/ezauthorizerefund.php
- Removed: shopaccounthandlers/ezcustomshopaccounthandler.php
- Removed: cacert.pem
- Removed: settings/shopaccount.ini.append
- Removed: settings/shopaccount.ini.append.php
- Removed: doCURL() and validateForm() from the gateway class
- INI file: ezauthorize.ini.append.php → stripe.ini.append.php
- INI section: eZAuthorizeSettings → Sevenx_Payment_Stripe_Settings
- Extension name: ezauthorize → sevenx_payment_stripe
